<title>USA: Lehman unit files for $4 bln certificates.</title>
<headline>Lehman unit files for $4 bln certificates.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Lehman ABS Corp, a wholly-owned subsidary of Lehman Brothers Holding Co, filed a shelf registration with the Securities and Exchange Commission to issue up to $4 billion in asset-backed certificates.</p>
<p>The proceeds will be applied toward the purchase of the mortgage loans, the filing said. The mortgage loans were acquired from Lehman Capital Corp in a privately transacted transaction.</p>
</text>
